The derivative retains the upstream copyright and license notices. Its material
changes are:

- adds an output mode that converts ordinary Fluentd records into OTLP logs;
- batches converted records into one ExportLogsServiceRequest per Fluentd chunk;
- preserves typed scalar, nested map, and nested array values in OTLP AnyValue fields;
- projects configured record fields into OTLP resource attributes;
- preserves Fluentd event nanoseconds in OTLP log timestamps;
- lets the existing HTTP and optional gRPC handlers export prepared log requests;
- retains the upstream OTLP logs, metrics, and traces relay path; and
- registers both the `opentelemetry_radiant` and compatibility `opentelemetry`
  output names.

The generated OpenTelemetry protobuf Ruby files remain derived from the
OpenTelemetry Protocol project and retain their embedded Apache-2.0 notices.
